WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:07.392
A chip brings processors, memories, and interfaces together inside one fixed boundary.

2
00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:14.586
Every block must appear once, stay inside the outline, and avoid sharing interior space.

3
00:00:15.676 --> 00:00:21.996
Legality is only the beginning; the same blocks can be scattered or packed tightly.

4
00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:29.910
Slicing trees, binary trees, and sequence pairs turn geometric layouts into encodings we can manipulate.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.680
Annealing explores new encodings, while soft blocks change shape without changing their area.

6
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:45.042
Next, predict the result, try the experiment, and use your own code to explain why.
